<section class="reference-section" id="krishna-govardhana">
  <div class="reference-section-heading"><h2>Krishna and Govardhana</h2><a href="/krishna-govardhana.html">Return to story</a></div>
  <div class="reference-content">
    <p>This original condensed retelling follows Bhagavata Purana 10.24–27. The Sanskrit verses and English translation in the Bhaktivedanta Book Trust edition on VedaBase provide the reference trail. This is a Vaishnava devotional edition; its explanatory purports are commentary, distinguished from the verses. No translation is reproduced at length.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/24/">Book 10, chapter 24</a><small>The preparations, Nanda’s explanation and the offering. Key verses: 1–12 and 25–34.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/24/35/">10.24.35</a><small>Krishna’s manifestation as Govardhana; also see 10.24.36.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/25/">Book 10, chapter 25</a><small>The storm and its ending: 1–18 and 24–33.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/25/19/">10.25.19</a><small>The verse describes lifting with one hand. The reader retains that wording; the edition’s purport separately discusses the left hand.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/25/22/">10.25.22</a><small>The community beneath the hill.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/25/23/">10.25.23</a><small>Seven days of protection.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/26/">Book 10, chapter 26</a><small>The villagers’ questions and Nanda’s recollection of Garga, especially 1–3 and 13–25.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/27/">Book 10, chapter 27</a><small>Indra’s recognition and return to responsibility: 1–17; the celebration and conclusion: 24–28.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/27/20/">10.27.20</a><small>Surabhi’s appeal; also see 18–21.</small></li>
      <li><a href="https://vedabase.io/en/library/sb/10/27/22-23/">10.27.22–23</a><small>The ceremonial bathing and name Govinda.</small></li>
    </ol>
    <p>The reflection on responsibility is editorial. The new cover and interior paintings are AI-generated devotional interpretations, each used once. Their imagined settings are not geographical documentation, and the interior is not a literal depiction of every detail in 10.27.2.</p>
  </div>
</section>
